  "title": "EU Fines Google $1 Billion for Prioritizing Its Own Services in Search",
  "summary": "The European Commission claims that Google boosted its own apps and products to the top of search rankings to the detriment of its competitors. This marks a significant step in the ongoing EU efforts to regulate digital market practices.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The European Commission claims that Google boosted its own apps and products to the top of search rankings to the detriment of its competitors.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The EU has introduced stricter rules on ChatGPT, Reddit, and Roblox, requiring platforms to comply with new online safety regulations aimed at protecting users from harmful content and minors.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The U.S. president has threatened the European Union with additional and'substantial' tariffs after the EU imposed a series of steep fines on U.S. tech giants, including Google, Apple, and Meta Platforms.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
